# Generated walkthrough + report page. Derived entirely from the shipped level data
# and the solver, and REGENERATED whenever a game rule changes -- a checked-in copy
# goes stale silently and then confidently describes shots that no longer work.
# Rebuild: assets/solvelevels.py --report, then assets/walkthroughhtml.py
**/assets/roundbook.html
**/assets/WALKTHROUGH.md
**/assets/walkthrough.json

# --- Generated preview renders (NOT reference art) ---
# BUST-A-BOBBLE's previews are 100% derived: prevlevels.py/prevcolours.py redraw
# them from levels.txt plus the same DEFINE CHAR/COLOR tables genart.py emits, and
# its actual source material is TEXT (assets/arcade-stages.txt). Git cannot delta a
# PNG, so one palette tweak rewrites all 31 and adds ~412 KB to history forever.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT a blanket *.png rule. Other games' PNGs are REFERENCE ART and
# must stay tracked -- games/HardHatMack/assets/HHM-*.png and RallyX's
# Rally-X-Level*.png / ref-*-arcade.png are arcade rips, the ground truth every
# layout was transcribed against. They are irreplaceable input, not output.
# NB: `**/` prefix, not `games/...`. This file sits one level ABOVE AI-Games, so a
# pattern starting `games/` anchors to the wrong directory and matches nothing.
**/BustABobble/assets/level-*.png
**/BustABobble/assets/alignment.png
**/BustABobble/assets/colours.png

# Classic99's own config, rewritten by the emulator every time it exits. Machine-
# local state (window size, stretch mode, MRU list), not project configuration.
classic99.ini

